            "reply_data": [
                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64155612?u=b4aa60589d92918092f4ed0843d31ce8c1768f47&v=4",
                        "login": "GitMurf",
                        "resourcePath": "/GitMurf",
                        "url": "https://github.com/GitMurf"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
                    "body": "Ok, but just realized that we can somewhat get around this by setting the window options in mini.completion config. For example:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n    window = {\r\n      info = { height = 75, width = 80, border = 'double' },\r\n      -- ... other stuff\r\n    },\r\n```\r\n\r\nAny issue with this @echasnovski ? it seems like it works nicely where the height is just the max, so when smaller it will shrink / size accordingly. This just allows for ability to maximize the potential size of the window on large documentation items.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Ok, but just realized that we can somewhat get around this by setting the window options in mini.completion config. For example:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    window = {\n      info = { height = 75, width = 80, border = 'double' },\n      -- ... other stuff\n    },\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">    <span class=\"pl-smi\">window</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">info</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">height</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">75</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">width</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">80</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">border</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>double<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n      <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> ... other stuff</span>\n    },</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Any issue with this <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a> ? it seems like it works nicely where the height is just the max, so when smaller it will shrink / size accordingly. This just allows for ability to maximize the potential size of the window on large documentation items.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Ok, but just realized that we can somewhat get around this by setting the window options in mini.completion config. For example:\n    window = {\n      info = { height = 75, width = 80, border = 'double' },\n      -- ... other stuff\n    },\nAny issue with this @echasnovski ? it seems like it works nicely where the height is just the max, so when smaller it will shrink / size accordingly. This just allows for ability to maximize the potential size of the window on large documentation items.",
