                },
                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "If this works for you, then great. I personally prefer not having completion popup and windows span across the whole height.\r\nYou can also set `height = vim.o.lines` (or `height = vim.o.lines - 3` to account for tabline+statusline+cmdline) and it may increase up to the whole terminal instance height.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">If this works for you, then great. I personally prefer not having completion popup and windows span across the whole height.<br>\nYou can also set <code class=\"notranslate\">height = vim.o.lines</code> (or <code class=\"notranslate\">height = vim.o.lines - 3</code> to account for tabline+statusline+cmdline) and it may increase up to the whole terminal instance height.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "If this works for you, then great. I personally prefer not having completion popup and windows span across the whole height.\nYou can also set height = vim.o.lines (or height = vim.o.lines - 3 to account for tabline+statusline+cmdline) and it may increase up to the whole terminal instance height.",
